From: Cidwel <cidwel@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_qg: distrust an S2 average above the design window too

Patch 0104 falls back to the last ADC sample when the hardware average reads
below the design minimum after a cold boot. Measured on 2026-09-05 the
average can also read garbage ABOVE it: 6.38 V on a 4.4 V cell, 17 s into a
cold boot, which this driver turned into a confident 100 % while the cell
was at 3.74 V. Fall back on that side as well, only to a sample that is
itself plausible.
---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_qg.c	2026-09-05 11:54:04.027155678 +0200
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_qg.c	2026-09-05 11:54:38.652862831 +0200
@@ -108,11 +108,22 @@
 	 * is valid from the very first moment. It is noisier than the average, and that
 	 * is why it is only used when the average says nothing credible.
 	 */
-	if (voltage_now < voltage_min) {
+	/*
+	 * And "I do not know" is not "full" either. Measured 2026-09-05, 17 s
+	 * after a cold boot: the S2 average read 6.38 V on a 4.4 V cell, so
+	 * this reported 100 % while the instantaneous ADC said 3.74 V (34 %).
+	 * Seven minutes later the average had settled at 3.73 V. So the
+	 * average is distrusted on BOTH sides of the design window, with a
+	 * margin above the maximum because a charging cell legitimately sits
+	 * a little over it.
+	 */
+	if (voltage_now < voltage_min || voltage_now > voltage_max + 100000) {
 		int last;
 
 		if (!qcom_qg_get_voltage(chip, QG_LAST_ADC_V_DATA0_REG,
-					 &last) && last > voltage_now)
+					 &last) &&
+		    last >= voltage_min - 300000 &&
+		    last <= voltage_max + 100000)
 			voltage_now = last;
 	}
 
